From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: count rx_packets before netif_receive_skb (0176)

netif_receive_skb() returns NET_RX_DROP for a frame consumed by the
NF_NETDEV_INGRESS hook, which is how the software flowtable forwards. The
driver counted that as rx_dropped and never as rx_packets/rx_bytes, so every
software-forwarded frame (flows not yet offloaded, software fallback, ports
without offload) was reported as a drop. Account the frame first and ignore
the return value. Vendor ASK patch 104 fixes the SDK driver the same way
(plans/ASK2-VENDOR-ASK-REVIEW.md R3).

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
index 3edc8d1..dedb3be 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -2825,14 +2825,15 @@ static enum qman_cb_dqrr_result rx_default_dqrr(struct qman_portal *portal,
 
 	skb_len = skb->len;
 
-	if (unlikely(netif_receive_skb(skb) == NET_RX_DROP)) {
-		percpu_stats->rx_dropped++;
-		return qman_cb_dqrr_consume;
-	}
-
+	/* NET_RX_DROP is also returned for a frame consumed by an ingress
+	 * hook (the software flowtable forwards this way), so it is not a
+	 * drop report: account the frame before handing it to the stack.
+	 */
 	percpu_stats->rx_packets++;
 	percpu_stats->rx_bytes += skb_len;
 
+	netif_receive_skb(skb);
+
 	return qman_cb_dqrr_consume;
 }
 
